# WT vs Documented Mutant ATXN3 Protein Sequence Comparison

Gene:
ATXN3 Reference transcript: NM_004993.6
Reference protein: NP_004984.2

Documented variant:
ATXN3 CAG trinucleotide repeat expansion
68-repeat expanded model

Protein consequence: Expanded polyglutamine (polyQ) tract

Mutation type: Trinucleotide repeat expansion / in-frame repeat expansion
   
WT protein length: 361 amino acids
Mutant protein length: 415 amino acids

WT:MESIFHEKQE...
Mutant: MESIFHEKQE...
Comparison: The WT and mutant ATXN3 proteins are identical before the expanded 
repeat region. The documented mutation adds 54 additional CAG repeats, and because 
each CAG codes for glutamine (Q), the mutant protein contains 54 additional glutamine 
residues. The reading frame is preserved because the added 162 nucleotides are divisible 
by three. Therefore, the main difference between the WT and mutant proteins is the expanded 
polyglutamine tract, while the downstream sequence and normal stop codon are retained.

